cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use swifttn93, please cite it as below, and also cite tn93, whose behaviour it reproduces, and HIV-TRACE."
title: "swifttn93: a byte-identical drop-in replacement for tn93"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-04
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/joe-b-christensen/swifttn93"
authors:
  - family-names: Christensen
    given-names: Joe
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0908-1299"
    email: joechristensen@clin.au.dk
    affiliation: "Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit (TNU), Department of Clinical Medicine, Aarhus University, Denmark"
keywords:
  - TN93
  - tn93
  - HIV-TRACE
  - molecular epidemiology
  - performance
abstract: >-
  swifttn93 writes tn93 v1.1.0's single-thread distance file and JSON summary, byte for byte, at any thread count. On
  three real HIV-1 sets at the 1.5% threshold, at two threads on an AVX-512 CPU, it was 25- to 30-fold faster than
  standard tn93 and 1.2- to 1.4-fold faster than tn93's filtered mode, -S, which reports the same links but summarises
  only the pairs that pass its filter. On an AVX2 laptop it was 6-fold faster than standard tn93, and -S was 3.5- to
  7-fold faster than swifttn93.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "tn93"
    authors:
